{"assets":["/statement-assets/1dbb33582b0834e2aa763431e2914259208249f176ec3714fb246ecc315a2a2f.png","/statement-assets/b30ab17eff427ac7ef7c6cf056ac6a52916dac103e069d8ba80c43d047a05742.png","/statement-assets/7da7b7f9c28e45a6f87e2396b295288277f41f8d9cbf8e374f5c8ba48696829f.png","/statement-assets/ec2d8b4d8a663dbfdd9182e4222fed6df801047824b3cc070e9b1e6ad2920b2d.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2111","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Puzzle"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have been gifted a puzzle, where each piece of this puzzle is a square with a side length of one. You can glue any picture onto this puzzle, cut it, and obtain an almost ordinary jigsaw puzzle."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your friend is an avid mathematician, so he suggested you consider the following problem. Is it possible to arrange the puzzle pieces in such a way that the following conditions are met:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pieces are aligned parallel to the coordinate axes; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pieces do not overlap each other; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" all pieces form a single connected component (i.e., there exists a path from each piece to every other piece along the pieces, where each two consecutive pieces share a side); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the ratio of the perimeter of this component to the area of this component equals $$$\\frac{p}{s}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the number of pieces used does not exceed $$$50\\,000$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you handle it?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/1dbb33582b0834e2aa763431e2914259208249f176ec3714fb246ecc315a2a2f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For this figure, the ratio of the perimeter to the area is $$$\\frac{11}{9}$$$"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test consists of several test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains two integers $$$p$$$ and $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le p, s \\le 50$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if it is impossible to arrange the pieces as described above, output a single integer $$$-1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" otherwise, in the first line output a single integer $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le k \\le 50\\,000$$$), and then in $$$k$$$ lines output the coordinates of the pieces: each line should contain two integers $$$x_{i}$$$ and $$$y_{i}$$$ ($$$-10^{9} \\le x_{i}, y_{i} \\le 10^{9}$$$). If there are multiple suitable arrangements of the pieces, output any of them. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 1\n31 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n20\n3 7\n3 8\n6 4\n6 5\n3 5\n4 4\n4 5\n4 3\n3 4\n5 3\n5 4\n5 7\n3 6\n4 6\n5 5\n5 6\n4 7\n4 8\n6 6\n6 7\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n4 2\n12 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n24\n-7 2\n-3 -3\n-7 -5\n-7 1\n-3 2\n-7 -2\n-3 -5\n-7 -6\n-5 -6\n-3 -4\n-3 -6\n-7 0\n-6 -6\n-7 -3\n-5 2\n-7 -1\n-3 1\n-4 -6\n-3 0\n-7 -4\n-6 2\n-4 2\n-3 -1\n-3 -2\n5\n0 0\n0 1\n1 0\n-1 0\n0 -1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case of the first test, the figure may look like this:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b30ab17eff427ac7ef7c6cf056ac6a52916dac103e069d8ba80c43d047a05742.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test, the figures look like this:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7da7b7f9c28e45a6f87e2396b295288277f41f8d9cbf8e374f5c8ba48696829f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ec2d8b4d8a663dbfdd9182e4222fed6df801047824b3cc070e9b1e6ad2920b2d.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the internal perimeter is also taken into account!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"2111F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2111/problem/F"}